<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="04108875-0631-50a0-af4a-45dc48fb9ad8" activityNameId="69580d90-911b-568d-9b97-4b0498d83e88" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, spoil from lignite mining, in surface landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, spoil from lignite mining, in surface landfill
na;
Synonyms: lignite mine overburden, lignite mine waste rock; 
UUID: e6c7fd1b-ca1c-45f5-8220-6d9594dd093e
Waste-specific emissions from lignite spoil leachate. Short- and long-term emissions to groundwater from rainwater infiltration leaching. Leaching by lateral groundwater flow not included.; Geography: Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of lignite spoil production in the world.
Location:  Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of lignite spoil production in the world.
Technology: Mechanically stable and revegetated lignite spoil backfill or heap.
Time period: Average lignite spoil composition from literature references. Transfer coefficients from prospective model, specific to lignite spoil.
Production volume: Approx. 8580 Mio t/a lignite spoil generation
Sampling: Disposal model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial spoil composition from various literature sources.  
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e6c7fd1b-ca1c-45f5-8220-6d9594dd093e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">GLO</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location:  Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of lignite spoil production in the world.</text>
        </comment>
